- id
	Identifier of the movie on TMDB, the same as movies_metadata.id (e.g. 862 = Toy Story)

- keywords
	List of the movie's keywords (objects with id and name): plot themes,
	but also information about the production (e.g. "woman director", "based on novel")

    [{'id': 931, 'name': 'jealousy'}, {'id': 4290, 'name': 'toy'}, {'id': 9713, 'name': 'friends'}, ...]

    id is the TMDB code of the keyword, name is the text.
    As for genres, it is written as a Python list (single quotes): it is read with ast.literal_eval, not with json.loads.


FINDINGS FROM THE EDA SCRIPTS


- Structure:
	46,419 rows, 2 columns (id, keywords). All rows have exactly 2 fields,
	no broken rows as in movies_metadata.
	All ids are numeric, no empty keywords field.

- keywords field:
	it can always be read with ast.literal_eval and it is always a list.
	158,680 objects in total, all with only the keys id (integer) and name (string).

- Duplicated IDs:
	985 ids appear more than once, for a total of 1,972 rows.
	983 ids appear 2 times, 2 ids appear 3 times (141971 Blackout and 159849, both with an empty list).
	The copies are ALWAYS identical: keeping one copy per id removes 987 rows.
	29 of these ids are the same duplicates as in movies_metadata, the other 956 are duplicated only here.

- Movies without keywords:
	14,795 rows out of 46,419 have the empty list []; counting each movie once they are
	14,340 movies out of 45,432, i.e. 31.6%.

	It is not data missing "at random": it depends on how well known the movie is.

	movie votes      without keywords
	0                57.0%
	1-9              43.0%
	10-99            23.7%
	100-999           5.3%
	1000+             0.5%

	So movies with few votes almost always have no keywords, famous ones almost never.

- Consistency between keyword id and name:
	19,956 distinct keywords. Each id always has a single name and each name always has a single id.



- Keyword with an empty name:
	the keyword with id 13091 has only '\xa0' (a space) as its name: it is used in 4 movies and means nothing.

- Same word with different ids:
	removing the spaces, 6 words appear with two different ids: the "clean" version and the one with the space.

	word             id       name                     movies
	infatuation      34262    'infatuation \xa0'       3
	infatuation      164500   'infatuation'            5
	telephone call   10904    'telephone call'         4
	telephone call   165803   'telephone call \xa0'    4
	tape recording   154904   'tape recording \xa0'    1
	tape recording   164543   'tape recording'         1
	bellhop          41241    'bellhop \xa0'           4
	bellhop          196267   'bellhop'                1
	poseidon         14667    'poseidon'               2
	poseidon         44365    'poseidon \xa0'          1
	hipster          155081   '\xa0hipster \xa0'       1
	hipster          175297   'hipster'                2

	For TMDB they are different keywords, but for a reader they are the same word: a query counting
	the movies with "bellhop" would find 1 instead of 5.

- Keywords repeated in the same movie: none.


